    "custom_faq_afKPpE": {
      "type": "custom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_73nVbP": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q1. What Does Anti-Spike Mean?",
            "answer": "<p>“Anti-Spike” refers to supporting a <strong>more balanced blood sugar response</strong>, especially after meals. The formulation is designed to support <strong>glucose metabolism, insulin sensitivity, and healthy blood sugar levels</strong> using ingredients such as <strong>Berberine, Chromium Picolinate, and Korean Red Ginseng</strong>.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_JYkk7R": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q2. How Does Berberine Compare To Metformin?",
            "answer": "<p>Berberine has been widely studied for its role in supporting blood sugar management and works through pathways involved in <strong>glucose and energy metabolism, particularly AMPK activation</strong>. Some studies have shown metabolic effects comparable to commonly used glucose-management approaches, which is why Berberine has gained significant scientific interest. However, <strong>Anti-Spike is a nutraceutical supplement and not a replacement for prescribed medication.</strong></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_Ei9q3J": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q3. Does This Help With Cravings?",
            "answer": "<p>Anti-Spike is designed to be taken <strong>before meals</strong> and may help support <strong>appetite regulation and sugar craving management</strong> by supporting glucose balance and insulin response. More stable blood sugar patterns may help reduce fluctuations that are often associated with cravings.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_PGmf7z": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q4. Does It Help Fatty Liver?",
            "answer": "<p>Berberine has been studied for its role in <strong>glucose and lipid metabolism</strong>, while improving insulin sensitivity and metabolic markers. Since metabolic health and insulin resistance are closely linked with fatty liver concerns, these ingredients may help support <strong>overall metabolic and liver wellness as part of a healthy lifestyle</strong>.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_f6D3Aw": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q5. Can Athletes Use It For Performance?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Anti-Spike may be suitable for active individuals looking to support <strong>glucose utilization, metabolic efficiency, and energy levels</strong>. Korean Red Ginseng is traditionally valued for its <strong>adaptogenic properties and fatigue support</strong>, making it relevant for people with active lifestyles.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_Ki3F9G": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q6. Does It Improve HbA1c?",
            "answer": "<p>Clinical studies on <strong>Berberine and Chromium</strong> have shown improvements in markers such as <strong>HbA1c, fasting glucose, and insulin resistance parameters</strong>. However, results vary by individual, and Anti-Spike should be used alongside <strong>diet, exercise, and medical guidance where applicable.</strong></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_kHNm3t": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q7. Why Add Korean Red Ginseng?",
            "answer": "<p>Korean Red Ginseng provides <strong>adaptogenic support</strong> and contains active compounds called <strong>ginsenosides</strong>. It has been studied for its role in supporting <strong>glucose metabolism, insulin sensitivity, antioxidant defence, energy levels, and fatigue management</strong>, making it a complementary ingredient in the formulation.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_yaGEHp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q8. Will Chromium Picolinate Help Insulin Resistance?",
            "answer": "<p>Chromium Picolinate is included because it plays a role in<strong>insulin signalling and carbohydrate metabolism</strong>. Research suggests Chromium may help support<strong>insulin sensitivity, glucose utilization, and metabolic health</strong>, particularly in individuals with impaired glucose regulation.<br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_VfcV3D": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q9. Is It Suitable For Prediabetics?",
            "answer": "<p>Anti-Spike may be suitable for individuals looking to support <strong>healthy glucose metabolism and insulin sensitivity</strong>, including those focused on early metabolic wellness. However, anyone with diagnosed conditions or taking glucose-lowering medication should consult a healthcare professional before use.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_HCkwHA": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q10. Can I Take It With Morning Coffee?",
